### Phase 12: Resilience4j in payment-service.
### Tokens:  ./infrastructure/keycloak/pkce-login.sh <alice|ada> 2>/dev/null
### Make account-service HANG (not crash):  kill -STOP $(lsof -ti tcp:8082 -sTCP:LISTEN)
### Resume it:                              kill -CONT $(lsof -ti tcp:8082 -sTCP:LISTEN)

@gw = http://localhost:8080
@payment = http://localhost:8083
@alice = paste-alice-token
@ada = paste-ada-token
@aliceAccount = paste-an-alice-account-id
@bobsNumber = paste-a-bob-account-number

### A transfer. Send it repeatedly while account-service is frozen:
### the first ones take ~4 s (timeouts + one read retry), then ~16 ms once the breaker is OPEN.
POST {{gw}}/api/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{alice}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sourceAccountId": "{{aliceAccount}}", "targetAccountNumber": "{{bobsNumber}}", "amount": 1.00 }

### Breaker state, failure rate, buffered and rejected calls (ADMIN)
GET {{payment}}/actuator/circuitbreakers
Authorization: Bearer {{ada}}

### State transitions and recent calls of the accountService breaker
GET {{payment}}/actuator/circuitbreakerevents/accountService
Authorization: Bearer {{ada}}

### Retry configuration and events
GET {{payment}}/actuator/retries
Authorization: Bearer {{ada}}

###
GET {{payment}}/actuator/retryevents
Authorization: Bearer {{ada}}

### Bulkhead and rate limiter
GET {{payment}}/actuator/bulkheads
Authorization: Bearer {{ada}}

###
GET {{payment}}/actuator/ratelimiters
Authorization: Bearer {{ada}}

### Metric: 0 = CLOSED, 1 = OPEN, 2 = HALF_OPEN (per state tag)
GET {{payment}}/actuator/metrics/resilience4j.circuitbreaker.state
Authorization: Bearer {{ada}}

### Health stays UP even with the breaker OPEN (details only for ADMIN)
GET {{payment}}/actuator/health
Authorization: Bearer {{ada}}

### Customers can't see operational endpoints → 403
GET {{payment}}/actuator/circuitbreakers
Authorization: Bearer {{alice}}
